    <briefdescription>
<para>Command history management using GNU Readline. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This module provides functions to initialize the command history subsystem, determine the history file path, load history from a file, and save history to a file.</para>
<para>The history file is determined by checking the $HISTFILE environment variable first, and if that is not set, falling back to $HOME/.sh_history. The history is loaded into memory at shell startup and saved back to disk on shell exit.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>pulgamecanica </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
